## 5️⃣ Optional Enhancements

| Feature | How to add it |
|---------|---------------|
| **Marker clustering** (when you have dozens/hundreds of users) | Include the MarkerClusterer library: <br>`<script src="https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/markerclusterer/markerclusterer.js"></script>` <br>Then push all markers into an array and instantiate `new MarkerClusterer(map, markersArray, {imagePath: 'https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/examples/markerclusterer/m'});` |
| **Custom icons** (e.g., user avatars) | Set `icon: 'https://example.com/avatar.png'` in the `Marker` options. |
| **Realtime updates** (new users appear without page reload) | Use WebSockets (Socket.io) or long‑polling to push new coordinates from the server, then call `new google.maps.Marker(...)` on the client. |
| **Persisting the current user’s location** | After `getCurrentPosition`, POST the lat/lng to an endpoint like `/api/users/:id/location` so you can store it for later visualisation. |
| **Filtering / searching** | Add UI controls (checkboxes, dropdowns) that filter the `users` array before creating markers. |
| **Styling the map** | Pass a `styles` array in the `Map` options (e.g., dark mode). |
| **Restricting API usage** | In the Google Cloud console, set **quota limits** and **billing alerts** to avoid surprise charges. |

---

## 6️⃣ Quick checklist before you go live

1. **API key restrictions** – only your domain, only Maps JavaScript API.  
2. **Enable billing** – Google Maps requires a billing account (you get $200 free credit each month).  
3. **HTTPS** – Geolocation works only on secure origins (`https://` or `localhost`).  
4. **Privacy** – If you store users’ exact coordinates, make sure you have consent and a clear privacy policy.  
5. **Rate limiting** – If you expect many requests to `/api/users`, add pagination or caching.

